        "original_id": "36220ead-6104-53e7-802e-aaa8d637a857",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Ehrlichman, Richard Nixon\n- Products: The Company\n- Concepts: Roman à clef\n- Events: Watergate scandal\n- Companies: Simon & Schuster\n\nFacts:\n- John Ehrlichman was a close aide to President Richard Nixon and was a figure in the Watergate scandal.\n- Roman à clef is French for \"novel with a key\" and refers to a novel about real life presented with a façade of fiction.\n- The Company is a political fiction roman à clef novel written by John Ehrlichman.\n- Simon & Schuster first published The Company in 1976.",
